      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Irregular pressure spikes in the hydraulic circuit usually point to issues within the transmission itself. Common culprits include a failing valve body component, contaminated or worn transmission fluid, or electrical solenoid problems. These fluctuating pressures indicate inconsistencies in the transmission's ability to control shifting force properly.",
