      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Inconsistent, intermittent behavior strongly suggests an intermittent mechanical blockage or a failing internal seal within the transmission. This randomness often occurs when debris is slowly moving through the hydraulic pathways, temporarily obstructing or releasing pressure spikes. Inspecting the valve body physically for hairline cracks or minute obstructions, or running diagnostic checks that monitor pressure stability over time, would be beneficial.",
